 we return the instance in the `playback` array or if we create a new one so we should go with the variant that uses less code, right? With that in mind the only difference I see is that in the case of an in-bounds but invalid stream we're not writing out an error message. The error message could help someone using this to debug their code, on the other hand they should probably check for a valid entry? I'm a bit unsure about this, so I'll go with your  expertise and remove the line + error message accordingly.","created_at":"2025-08-08T16:54:43Z","updated_at":"2025-08-08T16:54:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109381#discussion_r2263555994","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109381","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2263555994"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109381#discussion_r2263555994"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109381"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2263555994/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":267,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2259476636,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2263561404","pull_request_review_id":3101589503,"id":2263561404,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6G6zS8","diff_hunk":"@@ -262,6 +262,13 @@ int AudioStreamPlaybackSynchronized::mix(AudioFrame *p_buffer, float p_rate_scal\n \treturn p_frames;\n }\n \n+Ref<AudioStreamPlayback> AudioStreamPlaybackSynchronized::get_playback(int p_index) {\n+\tERR_FAIL_INDEX_V_MSG(p_index, stream->stream_count, 0, \"Stream index out of bounds\");\n+\tERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(!playback[p_index].is_valid(), 0, \"Stream at index is not valid\");","path":"modules/interactive_music/audio_stream_synchronized.cpp","commit_id":"1868ec223513b2113e3157c1bc214ea89c45d6c5","original_commit_id":"96269c4a724b457506719d3c669acdf73f363dbd","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It depends on if a null entry is valid at all, I think it doesn't matter much, but I don't know if a null case is reasonable or not, might be worth looking at other areas for that that do return it\r\n\r\nBut the only difference in user experience would be an error message, their code should still do:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar my_playback := get_playback(i)\r\nif my_playback == null:\r\n    return  # Or error, etc.\r\n\r\nmy_playback.do_stuff()\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut I trust what ever you go with, the error message would make sense if the payback being null is abnormal behavior","created_at":"2025-08-08T16:57:50Z","updated_at":"2025-08-08T16:57:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109381#discussion_r2263561404","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109381","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2263561404"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109381#discussion_r2263561404"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109381"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2263561404/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":267,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2259476636,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2264139874","pull_request_review_id":3102328351,"id":2264139874,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6G9Ahi","diff_hunk":"@@ -262,6 +262,13 @@ int AudioStreamPlaybackSynchronized::mix(AudioFrame *p_buffer, float p_rate_scal\n \treturn p_frames;\n }\n \n+Ref<AudioStreamPlayback> AudioStreamPlaybackSynchronized::get_playback(int p_index) {\n+\tERR_FAIL_INDEX_V_MSG(p_index, stream->stream_count, 0, \"Stream index out of bounds\");\n+\tERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(!playback[p_index].is_valid(), 0, \"Stream at index is not valid\");","path":"modules/interactive_music/audio_stream_synchronized.cpp","commit_id":"1868ec223513b2113e3157c1bc214ea89c45d6c5","original_commit_id":"96269c4a724b457506719d3c669acdf73f363dbd","user":{"login":"sebageek","id":2045907,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNDU5MDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2045907?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek","html_url":"https://github.com/sebageek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebageek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"So, I spent some time on figuring out when this happens: When we have a `AudioStreamSynchronized`, add two stream \"slots\" to it, leave the first empty and add something to the second, then we will only have `get_playback(1)` return a valid stream, the first one is a null object.\r\n\r\nSo this condition is something more or less under the control of the user (due to the arrangement of streams) and they can test if the playback is usable or not themselves. Getting a null playback might just be expected behavior when iterating over all streams. Therefore I'd go ahead with your suggestion of leaving the error message out. I also don't think we need a warning for this.","created_at":"2025-08-08T23:53:15Z","updated_at":"2025-08-08T23:53:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109381#discussion_r2264139874","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109381","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2264139874"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109381#discussion_r2264139874"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109381"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2264139874/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":267,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2259476636,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}]